fields.doc:
cost-price (cheng-jiao-jia) — true = cost-price SL (shared `isOpenPriceSl()`;
trigger == mother order price). DISTINCT from `is_limit_kind` (verified
separate controls in V1).

Pre-rendered "Hold positions" cell rows. Rust mirrors Kotlin
`PositionsUnitUtils.constructorPosValue` (`PositionsUnitUtils.kt:1343-1419`):
SPOT/MARGIN → 2 rows (assets + value);
EVENTS → 2 rows (contracts abs + value);
FUTURES/SWAP non-TradFi → 3 rows (contracts + coins + value);
FUTURES/SWAP TradFi → 4 rows (contracts + Lot + coins + value).

Native renders the rows verbatim — no inst_type branching, no
TradFi check, no `BigDecimal`. The Lot row is auto-included when
`OkSwapBiz::is_tradfi_swap(instrument) == true`.

InstId the sheet is opened for (Kotlin passes it in via `on_show`;
carried in state so `on_confirm` can attach it to the confirm UxEvent
without a second lookup).

variants.doc:
The write failed. `message` is the backend user-visible error (the
"cannot change with open orders / positions" rule is enforced server-side);
native toasts it. No local optimistic flip was applied.
